//! Push pipeline: ref-update decision logic and 14-step push orchestrator.
//!
//! Determines whether a ref update should proceed based on the force
//! flag and fast-forward status. Both normal and force pushes use
//! conditional writes (ETag-based CAS) to prevent lost updates from
//! concurrent pushes — force only bypasses the ancestry check.
//!
//! The [`PushPipeline`] orchestrator implements the 14-step push ordering
//! that ensures all immutable data is durable before any ref moves.
//! Individual steps are filled in by later tasks — this module provides
//! the skeleton and step boundaries.

